{"question_text": {"স্পেশাল বিসিএস (স্বাস্থ্য) - লং কোর্স": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Example of parasympathetic cranial nerve-", "option1": "Trochlear ", "option2": "Facial ", "option3": "Abducent ", "option4": "Hypoglossal ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Cranial_nerves_LMCQ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"784\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Unipolar neurons are found in-", "option1": "Anterior horn cells", "option2": "Mesencephalic nucleus of trigeminal nerve ", "option3": "Dorsal root ganglia", "option4": "Olfactory mucosa ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Neurons_LMCQ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"550\" />"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which is not true regarding glial cells? ", "option1": "Schwann cells electrically insulates PNS axons", "option2": "Astrocytes form blood brain barrier", "option3": "Oligodendrocytes have few processes", "option4": "Microglial cells are derived from neural crest", "answer": "4", "exp": "<strong>*** Microglia are derived from blood monocytes (Bone marrow origin).&nbsp;</strong><br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Neuroglia_t6NWKjC.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"649\" />"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) The white matter in the central nervous system mainly consists of-", "option1": "Cell bodies of neuron ", "option2": "Myelinated axons ", "option3": "Dendrites", "option4": "Neuroglial cells", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Grey_matter__white_matter_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"463\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) The cerebral hemispheres develop from-", "option1": "Diencephalon ", "option2": "Metencephalon", "option3": "Telencephalon", "option4": "Myelencephalon ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Brain_vesicles.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"406\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which of the following neurons are not present in the cerebral cortex? ", "option1": "Fusiform cells", "option2": "Purkinje cells ", "option3": "Betz cells", "option4": "Pyramidal cells ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<em><strong>*** Purkinje cells are inhibitory neurons characteristic of the cerebellar cortex.&nbsp;</strong></em><br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/cells_of_cerebral_cortex.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"800\" height=\"416\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) The term dominant hemisphere refers to the side of the brain concerned with-", "option1": "Perception & production of speech ", "option2": "Control of motor function", "option3": "Perception of visual stimuli", "option4": "Perception of exteroceptive stimuli ", "answer": "1", "exp": "*** The term <strong>dominant hemisphere</strong> refers to the<em><strong> side concerned with the perception and production of language/ speech. </strong></em>According to this concept, the left hemisphere is dominant in over 90 of people."}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Example non-capsulated receptor-", "option1": "Merkel's disc ", "option2": "Ruffini's corpuscles ", "option3": "Krause end bulbs ", "option4": "Pacinian corpuscles ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Receptors_in_skin.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"718\" />"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Which is the largest commissure of the brain? ", "option1": "Corpus callosum", "option2": "Anterior commissure ", "option3": "Posterior commissure ", "option4": "Internal capsule", "answer": "1", "exp": "<strong>*** The corpus callosum is the largest commissure of the brain. </strong>It connects the two cerebral hemispheres. It is 10 cm in length in man.<br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/White_matters_of_cerebrum.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"936\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) The genu of the internal capsule transmits motor fibres for the-", "option1": "Upper limb", "option2": "Lower limb ", "option3": "Head & neck ", "option4": "Trunk ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Internal_capsule_fig_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1000\" height=\"625\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Lateral medullary syndrome results from occlusion of-", "option1": "Anterior spinal artery ", "option2": "Posterior inferior cerebellar artery ", "option3": "Anterior inferior cerebellar artery ", "option4": "Posterior spinal artery ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Lateral_medullary_syndrome_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"404\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Choroid plexus is not present in-", "option1": "Roof of the third ventricle ", "option2": "Temporal horn of lateral ventricle ", "option3": "Roof of the fourth ventricle ", "option4": "Occipital horn of lateral ventricle ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Choroid_plexus_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"473\" />"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Which part of the face is paralyzed in Bell's palsy? ", "option1": "Contralateral half ", "option2": "Contralateral lower quadrant", "option3": "Ipsilateral lower quadrant ", "option4": "Ipsilateral half ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Bells_palsy.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"696\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Bells_palsy_CF.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"594\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Taste buds are absent in-", "option1": "Vallate papillae ", "option2": "Fungiform papillae", "option3": "Filiform papillae", "option4": "Foliate papillae ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Taste_buds_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"559\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Which is the artery of cerebral hemorrhage? ", "option1": "Lateral striate artery ", "option2": "Anterior choroidal artery ", "option3": "Anterior communicating artery ", "option4": "Medial striate artery ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<em><strong>The larger lateral striate branch of middle cerebral artery is called &lsquo;Charcot&rsquo;s artery of cerebral haemorrhage.</strong></em><br /><br />It supplies the <strong>posterior limb of the internal capsule</strong> which transmits <strong>corticospinal (pyramidal tract) fibres for the upper limb, lower limb and trunk.</strong> Hemorrhagic stroke at this region results in contralateral spastic hemiparesis.&nbsp;<br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/intracranial_hemorrhage.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"844\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Cerebellar lesion is characterized by-", "option1": "Resting tremors", "option2": "Ataxic gait ", "option3": "Chorea", "option4": "Muscular hypertonia", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Cerebellar_lesion_LMCQ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"549\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) In adults, the spinal cord ends at the level of-", "option1": "Lower border of L2", "option2": "Lower border of L1", "option3": "Lower border of L3 ", "option4": "Upper border of L4", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Spinal_cord_LMCQ_gPWJB15.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"926\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) The superior oblique muscle of the eyeball is supplied by-", "option1": "Oculomotor nerve ", "option2": "Optic nerve ", "option3": "Trochlear nerve ", "option4": "Abducent nerve ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/extraocular_muscles_NS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"404\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Taste sensation from the anterior two-third of the tongue is carried by-", "option1": "Lingual nerve ", "option2": "Glossopharyngeal nerve ", "option3": "Superior laryngeal branch of vagus ", "option4": "Chorda tympani ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Tongue_table.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"477\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Which is not a part of the basal ganglia? ", "option1": "Amygdaloid body ", "option2": "Globus pallidus ", "option3": "Caudate nucleus ", "option4": "Subthalamus ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Basal_ganglia_mhs.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"599\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) The circle of Willis does not receive contribution from-", "option1": "Internal carotid artery ", "option2": "Posterior cerebral artery ", "option3": "Anterior communicating artery", "option4": "Middle cerebral artery ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Circle_of_Willis_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"548\" />"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) The lateral spinothalamic tract carries the sensation of-", "option1": "Crude touch & pressure ", "option2": "Pain & temperature ", "option3": "Fine touch ", "option4": "Vibratory sense ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Sensory_tract_LMCQ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"455\" />"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Which is not a refractive media of the eye? ", "option1": "Retina ", "option2": "Cornea ", "option3": "Vitreous body ", "option4": "Aqueous humor ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<u><strong>Refractive Media of the Eye:</strong></u><br />From before backwards, these are<br />1. Cornea<br />2. Aqueous humour<br />3. Lens<br />4. Vitreous body"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Thin skin lacks the following layer-", "option1": "Stratum lucidum ", "option2": "Stratum corneum ", "option3": "Stratum granulosum ", "option4": "Stratum spinosum ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/skin_layers.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1064\" />"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) The limbic system is not concerned with-", "option1": "Food habit ", "option2": "Exocrine control ", "option3": "Recent memory ", "option4": "Sexual behaviour ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Limbic_system_functions_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"477\" />"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Which is a content of the cavernous sinus? ", "option1": "Internal carotid artery ", "option2": "Oculomotor nerve ", "option3": "Opthalmic nerve ", "option4": "Maxillary nerve ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Cavernous_sinus_MHS2.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"508\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/cavernous_sinus.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"449\" />"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Contraindication of lumbar puncture-", "option1": "CNS infections", "option2": "Intracranial space occupying lesion", "option3": "Subarachnoid hemorrhage ", "option4": "CNS vasculitis ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Lumbar_puncture_indications.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"896\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Lumbar_puncture_contraindications.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"578\" />"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) The cochlear duct in the inner ear has receptors for-", "option1": "Static balance ", "option2": "Kinetic balance ", "option3": "Sound ", "option4": "Rotational balance ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/iner_ear.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"696\" />"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Sweat glands are absent in-", "option1": "Palm of the hands ", "option2": "Areola of breast ", "option3": "Cutaneous part of the anal canal", "option4": "Glans penis ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Sweat_glands.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"369\" />"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) The thalamus acts as a relay station for all the sensory stimuli, except-", "option1": "Taste ", "option2": "Olfaction ", "option3": "Vision ", "option4": "Proprioception ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<u><strong>Function:</strong></u><br /><em><strong> </strong></em><strong>Sensory relay station</strong><br />A vast amount of <em><strong>sensory information of all types (except smell) </strong></em>converges on the thalamus and presumably is integrated through the interconnections between the nuclei. The resulting information pattern is distributed to other parts of the central nervous system."}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) What is the average volume of cerebrospinal fluid in adults? ", "option1": "150 ml ", "option2": "250 ml ", "option3": "350 ml", "option4": "500 ml ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/CSF_properties.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"780\" />"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Which is a purely sensory cranial nerve nucleus? ", "option1": "Nucleus ambiguus ", "option2": "Spinal nucleus of accessory nerve ", "option3": "Nucleus tractus solitarius ", "option4": "Superior salivatory nucleus ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/cranial_nerve_nuclei_mhs.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"760\" />"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) The maxillary sinus drains into the-", "option1": "Sphenoethmoidal recess ", "option2": "Middle meatus ", "option3": "Superior meatus ", "option4": "Inferior meatus ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/meatus_opening.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"227\" />"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) The skin over the thumb is supplied by the spinal segment-", "option1": "C5", "option2": "C6", "option3": "C7", "option4": "C8", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/dermatome_upper_limb.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"580\" />"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) The supraoptic nucleus of the hypothalamus-", "option1": "Acts as the hunger centre ", "option2": "Controls circadian rhythm ", "option3": "Synthesize vasopressin ", "option4": "Regulates temperature ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/hypothalamus_nuclei.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"423\" />"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) The lateral ventricles communicate with the 3rd ventricle through the-", "option1": "Cerebral aqueduct ", "option2": "Foramen of Megendie ", "option3": "Foramen of Luschka ", "option4": "Foramen of Monro ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/CSF_circulation_LMCQ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"871\" />"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) The parotid gland receives it secretomotor innervation from the-", "option1": "Submandibular ganglion ", "option2": "Pterygopalatine ganglion ", "option3": "Otic ganglion ", "option4": "Ciliary ganglion ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/parasympathetic_ganglia.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"850\" height=\"530\" />"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) All of these arteries forms anastomosis in the little's area of the nose except-", "option1": "Sphenopalatine artery ", "option2": "Superior labial artery ", "option3": "Greater palatine artery ", "option4": "Posterior ethmoidal artery ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Little_s_area.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"870\" />"}, {"id": "39", "question": "৩৯) Ape thumb deformity results from injury to the-", "option1": "Ulnar nerve ", "option2": "Radial nerve ", "option3": "Median nerve ", "option4": "Posterior interosseous nerve ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/main_nerves_of_upper_limb.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"853\" />"}, {"id": "40", "question": "৪০) Diagnosis of brainstem death does not require testing-", "option1": "Corneal reflex ", "option2": "Gag reflex ", "option3": "Planter response ", "option4": "Respiratory drive ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Brainstem_death.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1131\" />"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 6057, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "1800000", "is_omr": false, "omr_time": "7200000", "examname": "Oct 27, 2023", "type": "BCS-Health-Long", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}